# Family

A family is a shared group of processes, and by extention a shared group of projects that use those processes.

The basic concept is that you may have a set of processes for writing software and a set of processes for writing a novel, and this is a way to bucket them easily.

◇

attributes:
    - key: name
      name: Name
      details: The name of this family.
      rules: unconstrained
      type_spec: STRING
    - key: description
      name: Description
      details: A description of this family of processes.
      rules: unconstrained
      type_spec: STRING

associations:
    - name: Has Phases
      details: Ordered phase skeleton for this family.
      from_multiplicity: "1"
      to_class_key: phase
      to_multiplicity: any
      uniqueness:
          - to_attributes:
                - name
          - to_attributes:
                - num
    - name: Has Defect Types
      details: Defect types classified for this family.
      from_multiplicity: "1"
      to_class_key: defect_type
      to_multiplicity: any
      uniqueness:
          - to_attributes:
                - name
          - to_attributes:
                - num
    - name: Has Languages
      details: Programming languages used when estimating in this family.
      from_multiplicity: "1"
      to_class_key: language
      to_multiplicity: any
      uniqueness:
          - to_attributes:
                - name
    - name: Has Processes
      details: Versioned processes that belong to this family.
      from_multiplicity: "1"
      to_class_key: process/process
      to_multiplicity: any
      uniqueness:
          - to_attributes:
                - name
                - version
                - version_minor
